## NANO BANANA PROMPT RULES (apply to every prompt, every pin type)

- Always explicitly instruct: use the provided source image as the base for 
  this edit (Direct Inspo and Infographic pins that use a real photo). Never 
  use the word "uploaded" — say "provided."
- Always instruct a full strip-and-replace of existing nail polish/art before 
  applying the new design — no blending, no ghosting, must read as one fresh 
  manicure.
- Always state explicitly what must NOT change: hand pose, fingers, skin tone, 
  rings/jewelry, lighting, composition, framing (plus, for Infographic pins: 
  grid structure, badge/band shapes, font, text position).
- Always end with an explicit output aspect ratio instruction — Direct Inspo 
  matches the source image's own ratio; Infographic pins use 1000x1500px (2:3); 
  Informational pins use 1000x1500px (2:3).
- Text contrast rule (Infographic and Informational pins): text must never 
  match the color of the surface directly behind it — light text on dark 
  surfaces, dark/accent text on light surfaces, always.
- Informational pins only: no hands, no nail photos — text-card only, plus the 
  mirelleinspo.com watermark at the bottom, plus a CTA element.

